.TH elfshaker-esi-add 1  "elfshaker 1.0.0-rc1" "elfshaker Manual"
.SH NAME
elfshaker\-esi\-add \- Add packs to one or more remote indexes
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker esi add\fR [OPTIONS] <ESI_FILE> <PACK>...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add each PACK to ESI_FILE and every index named by \-\-also. Each pack must have an adjacent PACK.idx file. The command reads both files, calculates their checksums and sizes, and writes the fields required by each target index version.
.PP
The stored pack URL defaults to the percent\-encoded pack filename. Use \-\-pack\-url to provide another URL when adding one pack. An existing URL is an error unless \-\-force replaces it in place. All targets are validated before any target changes, and changed indexes are backed up unless \-\-no\-backup is present.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Replace an entry with the same stored URL.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-backup\fR
Do not write .bak copies of the previous index contents.
.TP
\fB\-\-also\fR \fI<ESI_FILE>\fR
Apply the same operation to another ESI file; may be repeated.
.TP
\fB\-\-pack\-url\fR \fI<PACK_URL>\fR
URL to store for one pack; defaults to its percent\-encoded filename.
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show informational progress and diagnostic messages.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIESI_FILE\fR>
Primary ESI file to edit.
.TP
<\fIPACK\fR>...
Pack files to add; each must have an adjacent PACK.idx file.
.SH EXAMPLES
Add one pack to a v1 compatibility index and a v2 index in one operation:
.PP
.nf
\fBelfshaker esi add \-\-also index.esi index.v2.esi release.pack\fR
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
elfshaker\-esi(1), elfshaker\-esi\-create(1), elfshaker\-esi\-list(1)
